--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Map data © swisstopo (Federal Office of Topography).
Source: https://www.swisstopo.admin.ch/en/terms-of-use-free-geodata-and-geoservices

swisstopo open government data is free to use for any purpose and requires the source
to be indicated. Generated maps carry this attribution in their metadata, and the
application displays it in the interface.

Datasets used:
  swissTLM3D          ch.swisstopo.swisstlm3d
  swissTLM3D Wanderwege  ch.swisstopo.swisstlm3d-wanderwege
  swissALTI3D         ch.swisstopo.swissalti3d
  swissALTIRegio      ch.swisstopo.swissaltiregio
  swissTLMRegio       ch.swisstopo.swisstlmregio
  swissBOUNDARIES3D   ch.swisstopo.swissboundaries3d
  swissNAMES3D        ch.swisstopo.swissnames3d
  Address register    ch.swisstopo.amtliches-gebaeudeadressverzeichnis
  Winter accommodation  ch.swisstopo.unterkuenfte-winter
  Ski touring routes  ch.swisstopo-karto.skitouren
  National map raster ch.swisstopo.pixelkarte-farbe
  Hiking/cycling routes  ch.astra.wanderland, ch.astra.veloland,
                         ch.astra.mountainbikeland, ch.astra.schneeschuhwanderwege,
                         ch.astra.winterwanderwege (Federal Roads Office, ASTRA)

The national map raster was previously listed here as "palette reference only". That
stopped being true in 0.2.0: the paper-map overlay (SPEC.md section 8.5) fetches
pixelkarte-farbe tiles and embeds them in a KMZ that the user installs on a device and
may pass on. Those tiles are redistributed swisstopo imagery, so the KMZ carries the
attribution inside itself, in doc.kml, as well as in the application.

Test fixtures and reference renders committed to this repository
(crates/s2g-core/tests/fixtures/, cartography/golden/) are small clips of, and renders
derived from, the datasets above, redistributed under the same terms with the
attribution in this file.

