Bundled third-party tools
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
These are fetched by vendor/fetch_tools.py and invoked as separate processes; they are
not linked into this program.

  mkgmap    GPL-2.0        https://www.mkgmap.org.uk/
                           Licence text: vendor/mkgmap-r4924/LICENCE (GPL v2, verbatim)
  splitter  GPL-3.0-only   https://www.mkgmap.org.uk/
                           Licence text: vendor/splitter-r654/doc/LICENSE-gpl-3.0.txt

Note on splitter's version (resolved 2026-09-07). This file previously stated GPL-2.0
for splitter, which nothing supported: the bundled r654 distribution ships
doc/LICENSE-gpl-3.0.txt and no GPL v2 text, its jar carries no licence file, and
neither the project's download page nor its documentation names a version.

Settled from splitter's own source headers, consistent across every file checked and
across two independent mirrors of the subversion trunk:

    Copyright (c) 2009, Steve Ratcliffe
    This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify
    it under the terms of the GNU General Public License version 3 as
    published by the Free Software Foundation.

"version 3", without "or later" -- so splitter is GPL-3.0-only, which is exactly what
the licence text shipped alongside it says.

This does not change anything about whether bundling is lawful. mkgmap and splitter
are invoked as separate processes and are never linked into this program, so no
combined work is formed and their licence does not reach this code either way. Under
GPL-2-or-later or GPL-3 the arrangement is clean; under GPL-2-only it would still be
clean, because there is no linkage. Resolving the version is a matter of accuracy in
this file, not of compliance.

  splitter's bundled libraries, per its own doc/ directory:
    fastutil           Apache-2.0
    osmpbf             Apache-2.0
    protobuf-java      BSD-3-Clause (see LICENSE-apache-2.0.txt and LICENSE-LGPL.txt
                       in that directory for the full set as shipped)
    xpp3               LICENSE-xpp3.txt (Indiana University Extreme! Lab licence)

